1
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:03,880
G-Girlfriend...

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:06,380
She's my girlfriend!

3
00:00:15,510 --> 00:00:16,900
It's a pleasure to meet you.

4
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:18,740
My name is Mizuhara Chizuru.

5
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:48,040
Rent-a-Girlfriend

6
00:01:50,010 --> 00:01:52,010
Rental Girlfriend

7
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:59,430
"The End of the Girlfriend"

8
00:02:36,610 --> 00:02:39,750
Wait, huh? Where's my phone?

9
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:43,310
Oh, I'm sorry. I must've dropped it.

10
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:56,730
Uh, that "rental girlfriend" just now?

11
00:02:56,730 --> 00:02:58,570
Why'd it look like Chizuru-san?

12
00:02:58,870 --> 00:03:01,780
Chizuru-san's a rental girlfriend?

13
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:04,570
Wow, is that true?

14
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:11,920
Th-That was a shopped image! 
We made that as a joke some time ago!

15
00:03:12,470 --> 00:03:13,580
Shopped...

16
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:14,630
...image?

17
00:03:42,030 --> 00:03:43,950
Rental Girlfriend

18
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:48,100
W-Wait, that's the actual website.

19
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:49,710
So it's true, then?

20
00:03:49,970 --> 00:03:52,830
R-Rental girlfriend means 
what I think it means, right?

21
00:03:52,830 --> 00:03:55,950
You go around pretending 
to be your client's girlfriend?

22
00:03:55,950 --> 00:03:57,880
Are you working that job, Chizuru-san?

23
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:05,650
<i>Wha...</i>

24
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:08,100
<i>Wha... Wha...</i>

25
00:04:08,390 --> 00:04:11,530
<i>What? No way.</i>

26
00:04:11,530 --> 00:04:14,810
<i>The secret's out? 
That Mizuhara's a rental girlfriend?</i>

27
00:04:14,810 --> 00:04:18,210
<i>Now, of all times? In front of everybody?</i>

28
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:20,070
<i>What's gonna happen now?</i>

29
00:04:20,790 --> 00:04:24,700
<i>Mizuhara can neither admit 
nor deny it in this situation!</i>

30
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:26,250
<i>What do we do about this?</i>

31
00:04:26,750 --> 00:04:30,210
<i>We're talking rental girlfriend here! 
It's not like she's waitressing at a café!</i>

32
00:04:30,210 --> 00:04:32,940
<i>They're not gonna hear she's 
working that job and go, "Oh, okay."</i>

33
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:36,610
It says you're number one. 
That's impressive.

34
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:38,400
Have you been doing this long?

35
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:43,450
<i>And Mami's attempt to cover it up 
only made things worse!</i>

36
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:46,390
<i>This is what you call 
a real sticky situation!</i>

37
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:53,520
<i>Calm down, man.</i>

38
00:04:54,030 --> 00:04:57,010
<i>They haven't found out about us yet.</i>

39
00:04:57,950 --> 00:05:01,150
Hold up. Did you know 
about this, Kazu-chin?

40
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:04,410
<i>I gotta brush it off.</i>

41
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:07,120
O-Of course I did.

42
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:10,330
<i>Don't let it show. Don't let it show!</i>

43
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:14,680
<i>Well, did it work? Did they buy it?</i>

44
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:17,050
<i>Crap, I can't look any of them in the eye!</i>

45
00:05:18,070 --> 00:05:19,910
Let's go, Chizuru.

46
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:25,060
<i>Mizuhara's totally panicking, too.</i>

47
00:05:25,060 --> 00:05:26,970
<i>We can't stay here!</i>

48
00:05:27,510 --> 00:05:29,930
<i>We gotta brush it off 
and act like it's nothing!</i>

49
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:32,630
Money.

50
00:05:35,330 --> 00:05:36,200
Huh?

51
00:05:36,870 --> 00:05:38,280
That money.

52
00:05:38,810 --> 00:05:39,650
Huh?!

53
00:05:41,020 --> 00:05:46,700
I saw you handing her a bunch 
of cash outside your apartment.

54
00:05:47,090 --> 00:05:48,280
<i>Dad!</i>

55
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:53,620
<i>Right, he did see me giving her money!</i>

56
00:05:56,330 --> 00:05:58,060
What money?

57
00:05:58,060 --> 00:06:03,510
I saw a handover of money 
between Kazuya and Chizuru-san.

58
00:06:03,810 --> 00:06:07,090
Why didn't you mention that, dear?

59
00:06:07,090 --> 00:06:12,130
I thought Kazuya was in debt! 
I told him to talk to me if he was.

60
00:06:15,230 --> 00:06:18,650
Wait. Does that mean the two of them...

61
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:21,250
<i>This is not good.</i>

62
00:06:22,190 --> 00:06:23,570
<i>They're not going to stop.</i>

63
00:06:23,570 --> 00:06:25,210
<i>The truth really will get out.</i>

64
00:06:25,950 --> 00:06:29,030
<i>Crap... I'm getting dizzy.</i>

65
00:06:29,030 --> 00:06:30,490
<i>I'm blacking out.</i>

66
00:06:30,930 --> 00:06:33,770
<i>Why now? Why here?</i>

67
00:06:33,770 --> 00:06:37,330
<i>I was all ready to put an end to it 
once we were back in Tokyo.</i>

68
00:06:51,150 --> 00:06:52,320
<i>Please.</i>

69
00:06:53,470 --> 00:06:57,650
<i>God... Buddha... anyone will do!</i>

70
00:06:57,650 --> 00:06:59,190
<i>Please just stop this now!</i>

71
00:06:59,670 --> 00:07:01,900
I'm sorry, you two.

72
00:07:11,330 --> 00:07:12,340
<i>Mami-chan?</i>

73
00:07:13,170 --> 00:07:16,240
I want you to be happy.

74
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:18,750
I'd never do anything to ruin your life.

75
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:22,710
I... I...

76
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:29,760
I can't cover it up anymore!

77
00:07:40,650 --> 00:07:42,610
Cover it up?

78
00:07:42,610 --> 00:07:44,860
Then it's true?

79
00:07:47,310 --> 00:07:49,940
<i>We're screwed. It's over.</i>

80
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:53,910
<i>There's no way I can explain 
the money thing away.</i>

81
00:07:53,910 --> 00:07:58,200
<i>And Mami-chan seems like she's 
ready to tell them everything!</i>

82
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:01,790
<i>Everything around me is fading out.</i>

83
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:04,710
<i>My whole world's turning upside-down.</i>

84
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,270
<i>It's over. It's all over.</i>

85
00:08:09,270 --> 00:08:10,460
<i>We're busted.</i>

86
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:14,910
<i>They know Mizuhara's a rental 
girlfriend, and not my real girlfriend.</i>

87
00:08:14,910 --> 00:08:18,770
<i>My brain can't process all this! 
My mind's going blank!</i>

88
00:08:19,150 --> 00:08:20,480
What's going on?

89
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:22,670
They're talking about 
rental girlfriends or something.

90
00:08:23,830 --> 00:08:25,760
<i>Now everyone else is catching on, too.</i>

91
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:28,650
<i>Duh. Our group's just 
standing around talking.</i>

92
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:32,710
<i>What about Kibe? Mom and Dad?</i>

93
00:08:32,710 --> 00:08:34,870
<i>What are they thinking?</i>

94
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:37,880
<i>Why isn't Gran saying anything?</i>

95
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:39,500
<i>Is she so angry that she froze up?</i>

96
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,500
<i>Or is she so sad that 
she's lost for words?</i>

97
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:44,330
<i>Or has she just lost all hope in me?</i>

98
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:48,580
<i>I have no idea what's coming.</i>

99
00:08:48,580 --> 00:08:50,580
<i>This is a total disaster!</i>

100
00:08:52,190 --> 00:08:53,760
Wait, everyone.

101
00:08:57,670 --> 00:08:58,810
Kazuya.

102
00:09:00,020 --> 00:09:02,370
I want to hear it from you.

103
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:06,360
Is Chizuru-san a rental girlfriend?

104
00:09:08,410 --> 00:09:11,910
Is she not really your girlfriend, then?

105
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:23,700
<i>What the hell? Why are you 
looking at me like that?</i>

106
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:25,610
<i>Why are you so calm about this?</i>

107
00:09:25,610 --> 00:09:27,710
<i>No... I can't find the words!</i>

108
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:35,640
After a year and a half, 
I'd finally stopped thinking...

109
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:39,390
that she was too perfect 
to be your girlfriend.

110
00:09:42,430 --> 00:09:43,720
I see.

111
00:09:45,110 --> 00:09:46,630
I see now.

112
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,860
<i>I can't do anything but apologize.</i>

113
00:09:58,750 --> 00:10:01,080
<i>I gotta get on my knees 
right here and now,</i>

114
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:05,490
<i>and I gotta tell her everything, 
even if she beats me black and blue.</i>

115
00:10:05,490 --> 00:10:07,390
<i>And I gotta say it's all my fault!</i>

116
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:10,320
<i>That's the only thing I can do now.</i>

117
00:10:11,150 --> 00:10:12,710
I-I'm sor—

118
00:10:13,930 --> 00:10:17,530
I'm so sorry, Chizuru-san! 
It's all my fault!

119
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:20,890
<i>Is Mami-chan trying to help us out?</i>

120
00:10:22,170 --> 00:10:24,810
You told me to keep quiet, and yet...

121
00:10:26,730 --> 00:10:28,790
What? Keep quiet?

122
00:10:28,790 --> 00:10:30,230
Chizuru-san said that?

123
00:10:30,770 --> 00:10:31,690
Mami-san?!

124
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:37,370
I can't, Chizuru-san! 
I can't deal with this anymore!

125
00:10:37,770 --> 00:10:40,870
I'm sorry for not telling you sooner, 
Granny Nagomi!

126
00:10:40,870 --> 00:10:43,080
I tried so many times!

127
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:46,330
I told them to stop doing this 
because I felt so bad for your family!

128
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:48,170
<i>Wait, what?</i>

129
00:10:47,210 --> 00:10:50,000
I told them to stop leading you on!

130
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,960
I knew Kazuya-san was paying money, too!

131
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:55,780
I just couldn't bear to see it!

132
00:10:56,210 --> 00:10:57,060
<i>What?!</i>

133
00:10:57,900 --> 00:11:01,240
I heard she even took 
your family's prized ring.

134
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:04,400
And he spent all his 
college spending money.

135
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:08,410
He even started working part-time 
to rent Chizuru-san out!

136
00:11:08,410 --> 00:11:10,570
<i>What are you doing, Mami-chan?</i>

137
00:11:10,570 --> 00:11:14,670
I told her over and over and over again!

138
00:11:14,670 --> 00:11:17,690
But she just wouldn't listen!

139
00:11:18,030 --> 00:11:22,490
She thinks she can get away with anything 
by saying she was being a professional!

140
00:11:22,830 --> 00:11:26,520
<i>What are you saying? 
What are you talking about?</i>

141
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:28,960
<i>You're making it sound like she's the...</i>

142
00:11:29,250 --> 00:11:31,580
But this is just too much!

143
00:11:31,580 --> 00:11:35,110
She did this knowing that 
Nagomi-san wanted a successor!

144
00:11:35,110 --> 00:11:37,930
Even though she had no 
intention of marrying him!

145
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:43,350
W-Wait a second, Mami-san!

146
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:47,770
What are you saying?

147
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:51,480
That Chizuru-san deceived all of us?

148
00:11:54,790 --> 00:11:58,440
I don't know if it was "deceit."

149
00:11:58,440 --> 00:12:03,660
But I think a year and a half is too long 
to write off as an honest mistake.

150
00:12:04,010 --> 00:12:06,420
At first, I jumped to 
the wrong conclusion, too.

151
00:12:06,420 --> 00:12:09,600
I thought Kazuya-san was in the wrong 
for continuing to rent her out.

152
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:12,670
That Chizuru-san was just doing her job.

153
00:12:12,670 --> 00:12:18,380
<i>Don't think you can get off light after 
wasting all those chances I gave you.</i>

154
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:24,360
But I heard she lied to her own grandma, 
and I didn't know what to think anymore.

155
00:12:25,370 --> 00:12:30,060
This all scares me so much, 
I'm even having trouble sleeping!

156
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:33,980
She takes money to hold hands,

157
00:12:33,980 --> 00:12:37,280
get food together, and go on dates...

158
00:12:38,210 --> 00:12:40,610
<i>It ends now.</i>

159
00:12:40,910 --> 00:12:46,160
Behind that smile of hers, what in 
the world is Mizuhara Chizuru thinking?

160
00:12:48,130 --> 00:12:50,200
<i>It's over for you,</i>

161
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:53,040
<i>Mizuhara Chizuru.</i>

162
00:12:53,590 --> 00:12:55,500
It's good to see you again.

163
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:57,630
That's a beautiful kimono.

164
00:12:58,090 --> 00:13:00,590
I've been wanting to see you.

165
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:10,980
Rent-a-Girlfriend

166
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:16,320
Room 301

167
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:16,320
Ichinose Sayuri

168
00:13:12,310 --> 00:13:16,320
What? You want to know how much 
Chizuru likes Kazuya-kun?

169
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:23,160
Sorry. They've been dating for 13 months, 
two weeks, five days, and 11 hours.

170
00:13:23,110 --> 00:13:27,790
That's quite precise

171
00:13:23,160 --> 00:13:27,790
I thought I might ask her grandmother 
how she feels about it all.

172
00:13:28,110 --> 00:13:33,700
After all, my angel is too good 
for that grandson of mine.

173
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:37,130
I still can't bring myself 
to believe they're dating.

174
00:13:37,130 --> 00:13:41,090
Please, Kazuya-kun is a lovely boy. 
You can be proud of him.

175
00:13:41,090 --> 00:13:44,220
You're the only one who 
talks him up like that, Sayutaso.

176
00:13:44,510 --> 00:13:50,240
But I'm sorry. My grandchild isn't one 
to be up-front about how she feels.

177
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:52,190
I haven't heard anything from her.

178
00:13:52,590 --> 00:13:57,150
How wise of her. Of course 
Chizuru-san would be that refined.

179
00:13:57,430 --> 00:14:01,090
Oh, no, she's just trying 
too hard to be mysterious.

180
00:13:58,690 --> 00:14:00,650
Her and her
high horse, gosh

181
00:14:01,190 --> 00:14:04,240
She's like a
rom-com heroine

182
00:14:01,930 --> 00:14:04,240
Enigmatic people are beautiful.

183
00:14:04,550 --> 00:14:08,640
This is the first time she's ever 
introduced me to her boyfriend, you know.

184
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:12,700
Oh, that's unusual in this day and age, 
especially for a girl that pretty.

185
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:15,600
Not that I know what she's 
been up to out of my sight.

186
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:18,190
She's very good at keeping secrets.

187
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:20,460
Oh, is she now?

188
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:23,950
Never mind me. It's not that big a deal.

189
00:14:23,950 --> 00:14:28,200
Either way, I believe 
in their future together.

190
00:14:29,060 --> 00:14:31,810
I can see it when they're together...

191
00:14:31,810 --> 00:14:38,020
The sight of them together, surrounded 
by our families and their children.

192
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:42,360
squee

193
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:42,360
squee

194
00:14:38,270 --> 00:14:40,960
You don't say! Me, too!

195
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:42,360
Right?

196
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:46,650
The coast of happiness is never clear.

197
00:14:46,650 --> 00:14:50,000
There are peaks and valleys, 
and demons in your path,

198
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:52,870
a path you might even 
lose sight of at times.

199
00:14:53,180 --> 00:14:57,400
But whenever that happens, my late 
husband gives me a kick in the behind.

200
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:05,630
"Don't stop believing. 
Never stop believing," he'll say.

201
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:10,220
Just hearing that is all too reassuring!

202
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:14,240
Let's bring in your 88th on Mt. Asuka, 
with the sakura in full bloom!

203
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:18,840
Yes, let's! I'm sure it'll 
blow my illness away, too!

204
00:15:19,330 --> 00:15:22,010
How many kids will they have? 
Two or three?

205
00:15:22,010 --> 00:15:25,050
What should we name them?

206
00:15:32,310 --> 00:15:35,680
Th-That can't be. 
It has to be some kind of mistake.

207
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:38,800
Chizuru-san would never 
deceive us like that.

208
00:15:40,190 --> 00:15:42,170
Right, Chizuru-san?

209
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:45,590
Hang on.

210
00:15:45,590 --> 00:15:48,720
Wait a second. 
Don't carry on like we're not here.

211
00:15:49,110 --> 00:15:52,090
Chizuru-san isn't really 
Kazuya's girlfriend?

212
00:15:52,090 --> 00:15:53,840
There's no way.

213
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:56,940
I mean, they've always been together.

214
00:15:59,650 --> 00:16:02,320
She stood up for Kazuya 
during that boozer,

215
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:05,580
and in Shimoda, he risked 
his life to save her.

216
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:09,910
Was all that an act, too?

217
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:20,850
And what's this about a ring? Is a rental 
girlfriend allowed to accept that?

218
00:16:20,850 --> 00:16:25,800
She even lied to her own grandma? 
What the hell is all that about?

219
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:28,260
Hey, Kazuya! Say something!

220
00:16:28,650 --> 00:16:30,390
<i>Kibe...</i>

221
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:33,160
<i>What is even going on here?</i>

222
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:38,200
<i>Are you kidding me? Why is Mizuhara 
being painted as the one in the wrong?</i>

223
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:40,310
<i>You know there's no way she could be!</i>

224
00:16:42,230 --> 00:16:47,240
<i>Why'd Mami-chan have to be so misleading 
after she assured me she wouldn't do this?</i>

225
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:50,340
<i>I'm sorry...</i>

226
00:16:50,750 --> 00:16:53,050
<i>I'm sorry, Kibe. Forgive me.</i>

227
00:16:53,050 --> 00:16:54,470
<i>I don't care what you think of me.</i>

228
00:16:54,470 --> 00:16:57,410
<i>But lay off Mizuhara! 
You're wrong about her!</i>

229
00:16:59,510 --> 00:17:03,500
<i>Why isn't Gran moving? 
Why isn't she saying anything?</i>

230
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:08,340
<i>Is there any chance she believes 
in Chizuru and lets this slide?</i>

231
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:16,160
Hey, Kibe!

232
00:17:21,610 --> 00:17:22,690
Please, no fighting!

233
00:17:23,060 --> 00:17:24,340
Calm down, Yoshi!

234
00:17:24,340 --> 00:17:27,150
Don't stop me, Kuri! 
I just can't accept this!

235
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:30,610
You don't have a clue, Kazuya!

236
00:17:31,070 --> 00:17:35,330
Nagomi-san was hospitalized 
before this trip!

237
00:17:35,620 --> 00:17:40,290
She was crestfallen she couldn't help 
Chizuru-san after she lost Sayuri-san!

238
00:17:40,290 --> 00:17:42,250
She was down in the dumps for a while!

239
00:17:42,750 --> 00:17:48,030
But she kept it from you because 
she didn't want Chizuru-san to know!

240
00:17:48,030 --> 00:17:49,480
<i>I had no idea...</i>

241
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:53,980
She believed that you would 
be the one to lift her spirits!

242
00:17:53,980 --> 00:17:57,720
She trusted you and waited all this time!

243
00:17:58,310 --> 00:18:01,550
I told you not to lie 
to Nagomi-san, didn't I?!

244
00:18:01,550 --> 00:18:04,150
So what's all this, you little punk?!

245
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:06,130
Pipe down, Yoshiaki.

246
00:18:08,610 --> 00:18:11,100
You're bothering the staff.

247
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:16,410
But Nagomi-san! It was all a lie!

248
00:18:16,410 --> 00:18:19,160
You were so sad...

249
00:18:19,570 --> 00:18:20,620
Never mind me.

250
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:22,580
But...

251
00:18:22,580 --> 00:18:23,830
I said, don't mind me!

252
00:18:26,670 --> 00:18:30,660
I'll be fine. I can get over this.

253
00:18:37,710 --> 00:18:43,180
Even if the first girlfriend my grandson 
introduced to me was a rental,

254
00:18:43,650 --> 00:18:48,650
even if the family's ring and our money 
were used to fuel a mere dream,

255
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:53,860
even if I've learned that those words 
and that smile were all a lie...

256
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:56,530
It was all too good to 
be true to begin with.

257
00:18:57,670 --> 00:19:01,910
One day, I'll look back and 
laugh at my own foolishness.

258
00:19:05,210 --> 00:19:06,510
<i>Gran!</i>

259
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:12,090
But the thing is, Chizuru-san...

260
00:19:13,170 --> 00:19:16,890
Sayuri-san believed in you—

261
00:19:17,510 --> 00:19:22,060
that her dear granddaughter introduced 
a boyfriend to her for the first time.

262
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:26,450
And I'm sure she believed 
it to her dying breath.

263
00:19:28,140 --> 00:19:30,720
If what Mami-dono says is true,

264
00:19:30,720 --> 00:19:34,820
then I can overlook anything but the 
fact that you lied to my late friend.

265
00:19:41,730 --> 00:19:44,700
I would like to believe 
that this is all a mistake.

266
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:47,570
Is there anything you can 
say in your defense?

267
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:54,960
<i>There's nothing we can say! 
Because we did lie!</i>

268
00:19:56,110 --> 00:19:58,890
I tried to, but she said 
she was fine either way.

269
00:19:59,890 --> 00:20:02,270
That if I wanted to talk, she'd listen,

270
00:20:02,270 --> 00:20:04,640
but if I didn't, then she 
didn't want to, either.

271
00:20:05,020 --> 00:20:10,200
When she said that, I just couldn't 
bring myself to tell her.

272
00:20:10,910 --> 00:20:15,200
<i>No! Mizuhara was torn up over it!</i>

273
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:18,610
<i>She just barely missed her 
chance to tell the truth, is all!</i>

274
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:24,550
<i>But whatever we say now,
after lying for a year and a half,</i>

275
00:20:24,550 --> 00:20:25,920
<i>it'll only sound like an excuse.</i>

276
00:20:27,050 --> 00:20:28,520
<i>It's not fair!</i>

277
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:33,800
<i>I mean, Sayuri-san isn't here 
to stand up for her.</i>

278
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:37,730
<i>There's nothing we can do anymore.</i>

279
00:20:43,550 --> 00:20:45,630
Hear me out, Mizuhara!

280
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:48,140
I'm not done here!

281
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:49,480
I...

282
00:20:50,350 --> 00:20:51,340
I...

283
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:56,730
But nobody in this world is a 
better match for you than him.

284
00:21:17,740 --> 00:21:18,970
I see.

285
00:21:20,230 --> 00:21:21,680
Never mind.

286
00:21:23,460 --> 00:21:24,480
We're done.

287
00:21:28,180 --> 00:21:30,200
I'm tired now.

288
00:21:43,550 --> 00:21:44,450
No...

289
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:45,580
No...

290
00:21:45,910 --> 00:21:47,800
You've got it all wrong, guys.

291
00:21:54,850 --> 00:21:59,520
<i>If you had to pick the worst declaration 
of love in human history,</i>

292
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:01,260
<i>it'd have to be this moment here.</i>

293
00:22:02,460 --> 00:22:08,310
<i>Before I knew it, that outpouring 
of emotion had escaped my lips.</i>

294
00:22:09,090 --> 00:22:14,870
<i>It was like charging into a gunfight 
with nothing but a matchstick.</i>

295
00:22:15,790 --> 00:22:18,800
Mizuhara's not that kind of person.

296
00:22:19,630 --> 00:22:24,280
<i>This pathetic white knight's 
final lie began to unfold.</i>

297
00:23:57,650 --> 00:23:59,420
Mizuhara did nothing wrong.

298
00:23:59,420 --> 00:24:01,340
This is all my fault.

299
00:24:01,740 --> 00:24:05,880
I don't care if people despise 
me for this or beat me up.

300
00:24:06,290 --> 00:24:09,760
But I swore I'd protect Mizuhara 
Chizuru from any and all blame.

301
00:24:10,390 --> 00:24:14,040
I could never bear to watch 
such a nice girl,

302
00:24:14,490 --> 00:24:18,000
a girl I love so much, 
be painted in a horrible light!

303
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:21,150
So there's only one thing I can do now.

304
00:24:21,910 --> 00:24:23,520
Next time on <i>Rent-a-Girlfriend</i>:

305
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:25,880
"Climax and Girlfriend."

306
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:27,030
"Climax and Girlfriend"

